uments point to a \"utility tender calendar\" for the amounts and the comparison with 2026. I couldn't find that calendar, so I can't say whether 2027 spending is up or down.\n- **Data centres:** Grid connection requests are expected to grow 9% in 2027. That is slower than in 2026 because power availability limits new sites. Demand is still growing, but at a slower rate.\n- **Order intake (VLTX holdings utility orders):** Quarterly orders have risen every quarter in the series I found:\n\n| Quarter | Orders (C$M) |\n|---|---|\n| 2025Q4 | 610 |\n| 2026Q1 | 640 |\n| 2026Q2 | 655 |\n| 2026Q3 | 670 |\n\n  That is about 10% higher over three quarters. The quarterly increases are shrinking, from 30 to 15 to 15. The series covers only VLTX holdings and ends at 2026Q3.\n- **Risk to the utility side:** Other nodes' documents show utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp. They also show two utility share offerings cut back in size in Q3. Node n3 is assessing whether utilities can finance their plans. Tighter funding could delay some 2027 spending, but I haven't verified that.\n\n**Gaps:** I haven't seen the 2027 capex amounts, the grid connection queue report, or any data on order intake beyond 2026Q3.","ttft_ms":3173,"type":"result","duration_ms":40846,"uuid":"8ac4d41c-a267-4bfb-ad08-b77ddf269cd4","ttft_stream_ms":1095,"time_to_request_ms":143,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":16,"resume_other":8,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":43,"input_hooks":1,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":13,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":17,"init_frame_send":5,"engine_pickup":4,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":9,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":2,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":2,"request_build":5},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":28,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":67,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process